<title>NETHERLANDS: Canadian judge resigns from Hague tribunal.</title>
<headline>Canadian judge resigns from Hague tribunal.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia said on Tuesday that Judge Jules Deschenes of Canada had resigned because of ill-health.</p>
<p>Deschenes' resignation will take effect from May 1. He has been a judge at the tribunal since 1993, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The tribunal's president, Judge Antonio Cassese, said Deschenes &quot;would be sorely missed. He has been an excellent judge, always showing the highest judicial skills, impartiality and integrity.&quot;</p>
<p>A nomination for a successor will be made by the U.N. Secretary-General in consultation with the presidents of the Security Council and General Assembly.</p>
</text>
